        "title": "Hydrogen Economy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Hydrogen is simultaneously the most abundant element in the universe and scarce as\na free fuel on Earth -- it exists bound in water, hydrocarbons, and biomass. The\n\"hydrogen economy\" is about manufacturing low-carbon H2 for roles where a molecule\nbeats direct electrification. The core challenge is not whether hydrogen is useful;\nit is where its cost, losses, storage, and infrastructure make sense."
